   "notes": "Cambridge University Press Bookshop (OSM node 1762331504), Trinity Street end at the St Mary's Street corner. Mapillary 934928010476370 / 1078821085942013: ground floor white rusticated stucco with one large round-arched glazed shop opening (modelled as a rectangular shopfront), white cornice band at ~4.2 m; above, brown-grey gault brick with two columns of 6/6 sashes with white architrave/cornice hoods and iron flower-box balconettes on the 1st floor, a blue plaque between; plain parapet. The real front looks wider than the 3.3 m OSM segment, so the two window columns are squeezed. Ground-floor stucco not representable (single wall material). s43: Mapillary 296497208762822 shows a slate mansard with one dormer above the cornice (no parapet); dormer added, matches the coincident way/137017430:1 annotation."
